meta {
  name: Stream master playlist
  type: http
  seq: 11
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/videos/{{videoId}}/stream/master.m3u8
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

docs {
  The entry point for a player. Any member who can see the video, READY only (409 `VIDEO_NOT_READY` otherwise). The variant lines are rewritten to **relative** API routes, so the player requests each rendition through the API too, with the same Bearer token.

  `Content-Type: application/vnd.apple.mpegurl` · `Cache-Control: no-store`

  Example response:

  ```text
  #EXTM3U
  #EXT-X-VERSION:6
  #EXT-X-STREAM-INF:BANDWIDTH=5640800,RESOLUTION=1920x1080,CODECS="avc1.640028,mp4a.40.2"
  1080p.m3u8

  #EXT-X-STREAM-INF:BANDWIDTH=3220800,RESOLUTION=1280x720,CODECS="avc1.64001f,mp4a.40.2"
  720p.m3u8

  #EXT-X-STREAM-INF:BANDWIDTH=1645600,RESOLUTION=854x480,CODECS="avc1.64001e,mp4a.40.2"
  480p.m3u8
  ```

  In a browser, hls.js adds the token with `xhrSetup`, but only for URLs on the API. Segment URLs already carry a signature. Try it with `npm run videos:play` and the "play through the API" link.
}
